  "task_id": "tmm_perform_one_bounded_tmm_thickness_optimization_f_d3f973237d",
  "user_request_original": "Perform one bounded TMM thickness optimization for an exactly 5-layer planar stack. Use the fixed material sequence from the incident side: Cr / SiO2 / Cr / SiO2 / Cr. Optimize only the physical thickness of each finite layer within the user-declared bounds. Do not optimize material identity or layer count in this route. Optimize a 5-layer spectrally selective absorber stack on aluminum substrate with material sequence: HfO2 | Cr | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2. Wavelength bands: 400-700nm maximize absorptance, 700-2000nm maximize reflectance. Normal incidence, unpolarized illumination. Thickness bounds: HfO2_layer1 [50-100nm] initialized at 68nm fixed, Cr_layer2 [20-50nm] initialized at 32nm fixed, SiO2_layer3 [150-300nm] initialized at 235nm fixed, HfO2_layer4 [50-150nm] uniform random initialization ±20nm around 80nm, SiO2_layer5 [50-150nm] uniform random initialization ±20nm around 76nm. Apply ±8% relative thickness tolerance for robustness evaluation. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with stochastic restart capability. Maximum 20 layers constraint satisfied. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Bounded thickness optimization for a 5-layer planar stack (HfO2/Cr/SiO2/HfO2/SiO2) on an aluminum substrate. Optimize physical thicknesses of layers 4 and 5 within [50, 150] nm; fix layers 1-3 at 68, 32, and 235 nm respectively. Maximize mean absorptance and minimize mean reflectance in 400-700 nm; maximize mean reflectance and minimize mean absorptance in 700-2000 nm at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Apply ±8% relative thickness tolerance.",
